{"title":"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems\">2002 AMC 12B #20</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">2002 AMC 10B #22</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Solution_1_but_shorter)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Solution 1 but shorter)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Quick_and_good_for_in-contest_use)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Quick and good for in-contest use)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29ab3e1eecd4bd8bb9c9d20855ffed7dfc40ffc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XOY$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> be a right triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/8532b6e341c7eb10b83b5bcd90694b09befdd41f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XOY = 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoints of legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a903f7c677cbaadb6e72741b95730648ab1d442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8afe773cd5709ee6b1f9f84680829802825cfab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OY$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, respectively. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/5/f85e7197a7c788037eb8467e08e0abe4bf026bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XN = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b1246265a664f64c58f6d7beb38c3635d154540b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YM = 22$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787261ea07bad10c79741dec56006870bfe5efc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 24 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 26 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 28 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 30 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2002_12B_AMC-20.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/57/2002_12B_AMC-20.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"453\" height=\"187\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcdcffa29ecf82ec37f53d9802ee5fb7b39eb74c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM = x$\" width=\"68\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc78fb8119ba4bc1003cf3b58239dfcc14b957b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ON = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c94d2aa0f4758455a6a8942881c387074409e294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XON, MOY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"17\" /> respectively,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d5e8b251c14deb1f13ca0546d6670f77b842fd8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (2x)^2 + y^2 &amp;= 19^2\\\\ x^2 + (2y)^2 &amp;= 22^2\\end{align*}\" width=\"128\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Summing these gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f7f134cc20466b92f0b2a0ae8caff320e1046a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^2 + 5y^2 = 845 \\Longrightarrow x^2 + y^2 = 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"274\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>By the Pythagorean Theorem again, we have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/41150d8d1a67090ffa4681e8ea5373efd66ddfdf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2x)^2 + (2y)^2 = XY^2 \\Longrightarrow XY = \\sqrt{4(x^2 + y^2)} = \\sqrt{4(169)} = \\sqrt{676} = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 26}.\\]\" width=\"598\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could note that since we found <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/fafeb40d05881e6f3cae2644e337548e7f20df18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />, segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bdad176347fc5753c956d2e8a8654ad5b03f0bc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />. Right triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/a/f4ac0cf3968a203aca43d97d0df5969ccadf68b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MON$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29ab3e1eecd4bd8bb9c9d20855ffed7dfc40ffc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XOY$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> are similar by Leg-Leg with a ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c84e3322f1ab5b8d7d7eebd071180aa98efeb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=2(MN)=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"201\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d27d91808d433beff1d107948b796f4e7f56ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XO=x$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c664e045b4776096b5ef2f3b7b8f2e05eda934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YO=y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/2066759e07851c69defb411eb4f28beda8ceaf07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"22\" /> \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036d7d36d4f971a35fd1c7a47de638519616822b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XN=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df21f17d1b16567ecf899fda01bd5791d58c614f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YM=22,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c410046f74f03d31da3f72e8dc8e0702040c760.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[XN^2=19^2=x^2+(\\dfrac{y}{2})^2)=\\dfrac{x^2}{4}+y^2\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d97369c237b3d4e29632c18df6e2aa47573c31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[YM^2=22^2=(\\dfrac{x}{2})^2+y^2=\\dfrac{x^2}{4}+y^2.\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Adding these up: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/7458c4588c0cc41f1fb658f988d1eb42da8b2a7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[19^2+22^2=\\dfrac{4x^2+y^2}{4}+\\dfrac{x^2+4y^2}{4}\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38ba20ebd3e2f790260ffea37cf840d7fc4e8f67.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[845=\\dfrac{5x^2+5y^2}{4}\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b445e92ac576c72926e2f9714fbb5c02fe6be8b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3380=5x^2+5y^2\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/2/d02e20b92d632ae6fc76b4025aedaafb2bf71cad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[676=x^2+y^2.\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>Then, we substitute: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9af3f7baa3cc1829cae4700366effa0159bab38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}=\\sqrt{676}=\\boxed{26}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"254\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Solution_1_but_shorter.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Solution_1_but_shorter)\">Solution 3 (Solution 1 but shorter)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Solution 1 but shorter)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Refer to the diagram in solution 1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/858ea809a9e7c8c42bcfff6528d096a681070a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2+y^2=361$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae70e023295c0dbc2852fb88ba2c4bcd5bb8613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y^2+x^2=484$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" />, so add them: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb110603e191672c72069962d1d637be2d4e7a3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^2+5y^2=845$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> and divide by 5: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c473a9451e6e14a77b82e3e4c4bf24702e0dfc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbfb4a5b0e469707e10c3d02887ba38035f0844f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{XY}{2}=\\sqrt{169}=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"146\" height=\"39\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626d05c7e840dd0b1aab43c0de05c306ea6d9824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=26$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" />, or answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69bb65d8b09333c4d5a11be52f4f7df860510d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"36\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the diagram in solution 1. Get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/858ea809a9e7c8c42bcfff6528d096a681070a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2+y^2=361$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae70e023295c0dbc2852fb88ba2c4bcd5bb8613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y^2+x^2=484$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" />, and multiply the second equation by 4 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dc0c46fbf95b4b82f96920a3595b51cef7c57c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2+16y^2=1936$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" /> and then subtract the first from the second. Get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f3f1a39ce9f813f035da059861ee657f9ff42b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15y^2=1575$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a402cdfc8cfed49a0affedba743fef8d6d831356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2=105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />. Repeat for the other variable to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d917e1982b7930b7419288b64fb94ecb7d18c41a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15x^2=960$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a4591fc9176c2eafcadc86e857e9e4aebce29afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />. Now XY is equal to the square root of four times these quantities, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46dd4eb5fae298a97cb5d53b7588dfbcb5198dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(105+64) \\cdot 4=676$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a11595d2f9312d3e4c35010ea0aba38388476f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=\\boxed{\\text{(B)}\\ 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"117\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Quick_and_good_for_in-contest_use.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Quick_and_good_for_in-contest_use)\">Solution 5 (Quick and good for in-contest use)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Quick and good for in-contest use)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711542e271632b40dd2f256c49b2ef74e4da93e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XM = MO = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f0996a4aa5aff8edd75506d044a787d282f06e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ON = NY  = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" />. Now, we can write some equations. We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/1/dc10e90765d673426c16c00d018c45956be4d90b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2y)^2+x^2 = 19^2 \\Longrightarrow 4y^2 + x^2 = 361,\\]\" width=\"289\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52d7351d7142c178e95638049084d3aa4e92ea9e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2x)^2+y^2 = 22^2 \\Longrightarrow 4x^2+y^2 = 484.\\]\" width=\"289\" height=\"20\" /> Adding the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equations up we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c500c094717b5cdd7ab2c881a46959af1a3ac70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5x^2+5y^2 = 845.\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"19\" /> The hypotenuse of the triangle is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4578d63cbd3ee14668ab0229d461611bc7be8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{4x^2+4y^2},\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" /> so that is what we want. In order to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d0454abb1e0f4d16be83b7d8d9a1971cc7bf6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^2+4y^2,\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" /> we need to subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/7/1c71397a41761fa3ae4bc83119c38cd495b29586.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/9/38970c3e07f022e794bc5387ac18a8fcad32dca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^2+5y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f62da1ed05b251695e48ae3ef68858725f179f89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2 = \\dfrac{1}{5}\\left(5x^2+5y^2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"191\" height=\"38\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253aaa00407e8a3d24673e95c87cd6b30209157e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^2+4y^2 = \\dfrac{4}{5} \\cdot 845 = 676.\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"37\" /> Therefore, the hypotenuse is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93a59a33a9acaf3b003d22160479d439562f39d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{676} = \\boxed{\\text{(B)}\\ 26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"128\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BIyhEjVp0iM?t=174\">https://youtu.be/BIyhEjVp0iM?t=174</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7wj6RupkO90\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7wj6RupkO90</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wik